    "summary": "Chief&#039;s mask made of wood. The mask depicts a human face with orifices at the mouth and nostrils. The face is extensively decorated in red, brown, black and blue/green pigments, including a red cross painted on the forehead. The mask shows traces of historic insect predation, likely to have occurred pre-collection. To the rear of the mask are the remains of hide ties that would once have been used to hold the mask to the wearer&#039;s face.",
